  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "If $B={3,5,7,11,13,15},$ which collection of subsets of $B$ is a partition of $B?$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $B$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $B$ where every element of $B$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{3},{5,7},{11,13,15}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${\u2205,{3},{5,7},{11,13,15}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{3,5,7},{5,11,13,15}}$ is not a partition because the element $5$ appears in two subsets.\n\n- ${{3,11},{5,7,11},{3,11,13,15}}$ is not a partition because the element $11$ appears in three subsets.\n\n- ${{3,5,11,13,15}}$ is not a partition because the element $7\\in B$ does not appear in any subset.",
